Polling vs Webhooks vs WebSockets

1. Quick Overview

| Approach  | How It Works                                                    | Communication   |
| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------  | --------------- |
| Polling   | client asks the server repeatedly for updates.                  | Client → Server |
| Webhook   | server notifies your app when an event happens.                 | Server → Client |
| WebSocket | persistent two-way connection for real-time.                    | Two-way         |

2. Polling
How it works

Client asks the server repeatedly every few seconds.

|----------------------------------|
Client → Server: Any update?
Client → Server: Any update?
Client → Server: Any update?
|----------------------------------|

Examples:
Order status refresh
Job/task status checking

When to use: 
Simple to implement,
but can waste requests
and server resources.

3. Webhooks
How it works

Server calls your endpoint when a event occurs

|----------------------------------|
Event Happens
     ↓
Server
     ↓
HTTP POST
     ↓
Client's Webhook URL
|----------------------------------|

Examples:
Payment success notification
GitHub push/issue events
Stripe payment/subscription events
Third-party system notifications

When to use: 
Event-driven & efficient.
Needs public endpoint, auth/
security, and retries handling.

4. WebSockets
How it works

A persistent connection is established between client and server.

|----------------------------------|
Client ←────────────→ Server
       Persistent
       Connection
|----------------------------------|

Both sides can send messages at any time.

Examples:
Chat applications
Live dashboards
Multiplayer games
Live delivery/location tracking

When to use:
When you need live,
interactive updates in
both directions. More
complex to build and manage.

5. Quick Decision

Need simple periodic check?                  --------- >    Use POLLING
Need server-to-server event notification?    --------- >    Use WEBHOOK
Need live two-way communication?             --------- >    Use WEBSOCKET
